      "writtenOn": "2022-11-22T22:14:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, what I mean is that USB4 entry doesn\u0027t use anything to from either Discover SVIDs/MODEs messages in terms of what communicates USB4 support. USB4 support is communicated only in Discover Identity VDOs.\n\nBut, we always attempt Discover SVID/Modes as a DFP and so if the port partner doesn\u0027t reply to those messages, then our end won\u0027t attempt USB4 entry because this check is required to pass prior to attempting USB4, TBT, or DP entry.\n\t/*\n\t * If discovery has not occurred for modes, do not attempt to switch\n\t * to alt mode.\n\t */\n\tif (pd_get_svids_discovery(port, TCPCI_MSG_SOP) !\u003d PD_DISC_COMPLETE ||\n\t    pd_get_modes_discovery(port, TCPCI_MSG_SOP) !\u003d PD_DISC_COMPLETE)\n\t\treturn;\n\t\t\n\nSo my comment is more to point out that the test is adding Discover SVID/MODE responses here so this check will pass, but the contents of what\u0027s in these messages are really a don\u0027t care from the perspective of USB4 entry",
      "parentUuid": "50f2aee3_aaef7506",
      "revId": "b9bb3284e073585d1ce07d994259c98f0d14da55",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
